# Build context: only what is needed to compile, and only what must not end up
# inside the image. In a remote build the context is the repo clone, but a
# local `docker build` uses the whole directory: without these ignores a stale
# dev.db or a .env with secrets would be baked into the image. `.git` stays
# ignored on purpose (smaller context, no history inside the image): the build
# stage still tries `git describe`, but a local build reports `dev` unless the
# version is passed explicitly with --build-arg VERSION=... (CI does that).
.git
.github
.codegraph
bin/
tmp/
uploads/
*.db*
.env
docs/
bruno/
scripts/
README.md
AGENTS.md
